-family:Georgia,serif;line-height:1.55">We present Omni, a unified multimod=
al model natively trained on diverse modalities, including text, images, vi=
deos, 3D geometry, and hidden representations. We find that such training e=
nables Context Unrolling, where the model explicitly reasons across multipl=
e modal representations before producing predictions. This process enables =
the model to aggregate complementary information across heterogeneous modal=
ities, facilitating a more faithful approximation of the shared multimodal =
knowledge manifold and improving downstream reasoning fidelity. As a result=
, Omni achieves strong performance on both multimodal generation and unders=
tanding benchmarks, while demonstrating advanced multimodal reasoning capab=
ilities, including in-context generation of text, image, video, and 3D geom=
etry.</div></details><div style=3D"margin-top:8px"><span style=3D"color:#25=
